   "cat": "Agreements",
   "when": "2026-09-07 17:09",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "Here is a concise equity-research summary of the filing:\n\n### 1. Most Important Fact\nSwiggy Limited\u2019s wholly owned subsidiary, Swiggy Networks Limited (SNL), has agreed to transfer its B2B authorized distribution business to step-down subsidiary Lynks Logistics Limited, and subsequently sell 100% of Lynks to Singapore-based Trustroot Internet Private Limited (TIPL) via a share swap for Series R CCPS.\n\n### 2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated\n* **Consideration:** SNL will receive **166,534 Series R Compulsorily Convertible Preference Shares (CCPS)** in TIPL at an issue price of **USD 314.40 per CCPS** (~USD 52.36 million total transaction value).\n* **Lynks Logistics Financials (Standalone FY ended March 31, 2026):**\n  * Standalone Revenue: **Nil**\n  * Standalone Net Worth: **Negative \u20b911 lakh**\n* **Transferred B2B Distribution Business Financials (FY ended March 31, 2026):**\n  * Revenue: **\u20b9668 crore** (representing **2.90%** of Swiggy\u2019s consolidated revenue).\n  * Net Assets: **\u20b9500 crore** (representing **2.73%** of Swiggy\u2019s consolidated net worth).\n\n### 3. Management Guidance / Forward Statements\n* The expected date of completion of the sale/disposal is **October 22, 2026**, subject to the fulfillment of conditions precedent and customary closing conditions.\n* Upon completion, Lynks Logistics Limited will cease to be a subsidiary / step-down subsidiary of Swiggy.\n\n### 4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On\n* **Closing confirmation:** Watch for the closing of the transaction by the targeted completion date of **October 22, 2026**.\n* **Portfolio value / strategic impact:** Assess the dilution of ~2.9% top-line consolidated revenue in exchange for an equity-linked holding (CCPS) in TIPL (a cash-and-carry wholesale player).\n\n### 5. Net Read\n* **Neutral to slightly positive:** It streamlines Swiggy's core operations by offloading a low-margin B2B distribution business in exchange for convertible equity in an international wholesale entity (~USD 52.4M), with minimal disruption to core quick-commerce/food delivery operations."
